Z||000005||qwikgta||09-22-2001||10:55 PM||||Bigred, Im sure you know this but i have to put it out again, the vents on the hood are for venting heat out of the engine bay. Pontiac engineers made it so that air going under the car will get sucked up into the engine bay and go out the vents.  If you block them and try to force air into them you run the risk of overheating the engine.  Now if they are for show then nevermind<P>Rob||||reg||1
